# Merges, tags, releases

A green PR into `beta` is ready to land. Agents squash-merge it themselves; promoting to `main`, tagging, and releasing stay on Jeremy's say:

- **Beta first:** every new feature and fix PR, from every bot (Cursor, Claude, GrokHub), targets `beta`. `beta` moves to `main` only on Jeremy's say, as one squash-merged `beta` → `main` PR. A hotfix goes to `main` only on his say, and `main` is then merged back into `beta` (merge commit, no force).

- **Green and ready:** Linux and Windows CI pass (find the cause before at most one rerun), and the PR body carries the proof of work, the base branch and its starting SHA, and a Skipped / not verified section. Report the PR link, the starting base SHA, the head SHA, and the CI run and its results, then squash-merge into `beta` (next bullet).
- **Merge into beta on green:** every agent squash-merges its own PR into `beta` as soon as CI is green; no human-review hold (Jeremy, 2026-10-24; confirmed 2026-10-25). **Never** promote `beta` to `main`, push to `main`, tag, or release without Jeremy's explicit say.
- **Latest base branch:** the base is `beta` for feature and fix PRs and `main` for hotfixes and the promotion. Fetch origin and re-check that the branch holds the latest base before reporting it ready, right before merging, and again before a tag he asked for; merge the base in first when it doesn't, and get it green again. Name the base branch and its starting SHA in the PR body and the report.
- **Merge:** squash and merge into `beta` on green, in stack order. Leave PRs he has parked open and untouched. Merges to `main` only on his say.
- **Main CI** must pass after a merge before any tag he asked for (find the cause before at most one rerun).
- **Tag and release**, only when he says: tag `vX.Y.Z` at the bumped commit on `main` (a promotion or a hotfix) and `git push origin vX.Y.Z`; `.github/workflows/release.yml` publishes the Release. Check the Linux tarball, Windows setup `.exe`, and Windows zip are attached and non-empty, write the notes, mark it Latest, and report the live Release link, asset sizes, PR and merge commit, main CI run, and Skipped / not verified.
- **Branches:** delete your own merged PR branch. Never force-push or push to `main`.
- **Versions:** PRs into `beta` don't bump — add `changelog.d/<slug>.md`; promotions run `cargo xtask bump`. Semver (Jeremy, 2026-10-09): **PATCH** (`x.y.Z`) is a fix or polish rollout; **MINOR** (`x.Y.0`, patch back to 0) is a promotion with at least one new user-facing feature; **MAJOR** (`X.0.0`) is a big milestone, only on Jeremy's say. No cap on any part (`2.10.99` was followed by `2.11.0` because it added features, not because of a cap). Each `beta` → `main` promotion carries exactly one bump (PATCH or MINOR by that rule) and one release. A hotfix to `main` is a PATCH bump and is merged back into `beta`. Beta builds carry `-beta.N` (e.g. `2.11.0-beta.3`) so beta never burns release numbers: `VERSION` stays plain and `crates/grokhub-app/build.rs` labels `GrokHub X.Y.Z-beta.N (beta @ sha)` with N = commits since the newest stable `vX.Y.Z` tag; never edit the Cargo version for it. The file list is in `repo-gates.mdc`. Docs (`README.md`, `/help` text, specs under `docs/`) must match what ships.

"Don't ship it", "hold", or a PR he names as parked means leave it, its branch, and tags alone.

## Branch cleanup
- Delete your own head branch after merge/close; delete scratch ASAP; never delete main/beta.
- Auto-delete head branches on GitHub when the setting is on.

